4/checkpoint/cp-build-344d41a8de18838e2902609aa1f4b9cbbcf66c476683aa645b0271681c668251/710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968","revision":"710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968","taskId":"cp-build"},{"ref":"refs/tally/spec-build/v1/9580b7cc868de0369023d414/checkpoint/cp-smoke-344d41a8de18838e2902609aa1f4b9cbbcf66c476683aa645b0271681c668251/710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968","revision":"710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968","taskId":"cp-smoke"},{"ref":"refs/tally/spec-build/v1/9580b7cc868de0369023d414/checkpoint/cp-proxy-344d41a8de18838e2902609aa1f4b9cbbcf66c476683aa645b0271681c668251/710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968","revision":"710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968","taskId":"cp-proxy"}],"remaining":["cp-tp2","cp-bench","cp-close","cp-usb4stream","rocm10-probe"],"frontier":[],"diagnoses":[{"attempt":1,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/60","diagnosis":"Blocked cp-tp2: the checkpoint requires a live two-node pair, and the second node is physically unreachable from the execution host, so no change inside the task's authorized paths can make it pass. Evidence: (1) host/fn-env.sh reported \"rail thunderbolt0 absent on this node\" and \"rail thunderbolt1 absent on this node\" — not dark-but-addressed rails, but no thunderbolt netdevs at all — then took the terminal wire fallback to enp191s0; (2) the execution host's interfaces are only lo (carrying 10.99.9.1/32), wlp192s0 (10.42.0.2/24, wifi), and tailscale0 — enp191s0, the 5GbE wire the fallback just named, does not exist here either, so even the declared fallback transport is phantom; (3) scripts/run-tp2.sh reached its first step, \"run-tp2: preflight\", and host/fn-preflight.sh died on its very first remote action (worker() -> ssh \"$FN_WORKER_HOST\") with \"ssh: connect to host 10.99.9.2 port 22: No route to host\", exit 255 — the ssh transport code, propagated by set -euo pipefail. Route lookup for 10.99.9.2 resolves via the wifi default gateway 10.42.0.1, i.e. there is no fleet path to the worker at all. The worklist is coherent and the code is not at fault: FN_WORKER_HOST=10.99.9.2 is the documented stable fleet identity (host/fn-env.sh line 49, handoff/PREARM-REBOOT.md), and preflight is correct to fail closed rather than fabricate a single-node first-light receipt. No receipt was written, so results/receipts holds only build.json, weights-coordinator.json and weights-worker.json (the latter dated 2026-08-29, when the pair was still reachable) and results/receipts/failed does not exist. This is an out-of-task infrastructure precondition: the coordinator box is not in its paired state (no thunderbolt rails, no 5GbE wire) and the worker at 10.99.9.2 is down or off-fleet, consistent with handoff/PREARM-REBOOT.md recording the coordinator as \"staged and awaiting its operator-supervised reboot\". Operator action needed before cp-tp2 can be attempted again: complete the pre-arm reboot, confirm thunderbolt0 carries 10.99.0.1/30 with a live peer and that the 5GbE identity 10.99.9.1/10.99.9.2 is up, then verify ssh 10.99.9.2 answers. A repo-side amendment would only be able to weaken the checkpoint into a single-node run, which would falsify the pair first-light, residency, fidelity, and full-context claims cp-tp2 exists to prove, so no proposal is offered. This is not a machinery or session fault, so it should not consume the machinery-retry budget, and cp-tp2 is a checkpoint, which never retries.\n\nCheckpoint capture: /home/tom/.local/state/tally/capture/archive/01a052f5-1872-7642-87ac-d37cdc1358be.cp-tp2/checkpoint.json","taskId":"cp-tp2","verdict":"blocked"}],"retries":[],"outcomes":[],"deferrals":[],"blocked":[{"blockedBy":["cp-tp2"],"taskId":"cp-tp2"},{"blockedBy":["cp-tp2"],"taskId":"cp-bench"},{"blockedBy":["cp-tp2"],"taskId":"cp-close"},{"blockedBy":["cp-tp2"],"taskId":"cp-usb4stream"},{"blockedBy":["cp-tp2"],"taskId":"rocm10-probe"}],"quiescent":true,"escalation":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/61","closingSummary":null,"warnings":["campaign pardon local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/44 pardoned 1 earlier machine receipt(s) for task(s) 'cp-weights', 'proxy-tooling'"]},"maintenance":{"blockingJobs":[],"cleaned":["pass:/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/.state/passes/fbea9b7290f2.json"],"currentRunHash":"2a4d73e64f52","liveRuns":[],"warnings":[]},"checkpoints":[],"merged":[],"published":{"action":"already-published","baseBranch":"main","integrationHead":"710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968","provenHead":"710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968","reason":"the gate-proven head 710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968 is already reachable from main","receipt":{"actor":"spec-build-driver","baseBranch":"main","campaign":"flashnext","provenBy":{"reference":"refs/tally/spec-build/v1/9580b7cc868de0369023d414/checkpoint/cp-weights-344d41a8de18838e2902609aa1f4b9cbbcf66c476683aa645b0271681c668251/710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968","taskId":"cp-weights"},"schemaVersion":1,"sha":"710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968","writtenAt":"2026-08-30T13:58:56.294Z"},"receiptRef":"refs/tally/spec-build/v1/9580b7cc868de0369023d414/publish/710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968","regateRequired":false,"sha":"710ee52011cf77c20dc96688a43530d117ebf968"},"failures":[],"diagnoses":[],"retries":[],"outcomes":[],"deferrals":[],"continuation":null,"escalation":null}}}
